hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1661","Narrated to us Bundar and Abu Musa, who said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubaidullah, who informed me Nafi', from Ibn Umar (RA), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said during the expedition of Khaybar: ""Whoever eats from this plant, meaning garlic, must not come to the mosques.""
Bundar also reported: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us Ubaidullah, who reported directly from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""Whoever eats from this plant, must not approach the mosques."""
"1662","Narrated to us Humaid ibn al-Rabi' al-Khazzaz, who said: Ma'n ibn 'Isa narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, from 'Abbad ibn Tamim, from his paternal uncle, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Whoever eats from this plant (garlic), let him not harm us with it in this mosque of ours.""

**CHAPTER:**"
